  "body": "### Describe the feature or problem you’d like to solve\n\n`gh attestation verify` currently insists on a token / authentication to be given.\nNow, I have a scripting codebase which – somewhere in its depths – needs to run `gh attestation verify`. Exposing a token to all of that codebase really isn't ideal in terms of security.\n\n### Proposed solution\n\nAttestation verification should work without token for public repositories (similar to how downloading release artifacts does not require a token).\n\nThis will benefit workflow users particularly when verification is nested in a larger codebase, and end users who just want to verify an attestation but may not have authentication set up, or not even have a GitHub account.\n\nIt would also benefit downstreams who run our setup in a workflow, because the need for a token is unexpected.\n\n### Additional context\n\nN/A",
